# RULE 50 — USMCA: ALL FLAGS ON EXCEPT QUICKBOOKS (owner ruling 2026-09-07)

Owner, verbatim: **"make this a permanent rule, all flags are on, except quickbooks and block. do it now."**

This supersedes any older doc, memory, or default that treats USMCA money posting as flag-gated OFF.

## The rule (LAW)

For USMCA (`operating_company_id = '5c854333-6ea5-4faa-af31-67cb272fef80'`):

1. **Every `lib.feature_flags` flag is ENABLED** via an operating-company override in
   `lib.feature_flag_overrides` (`user_uuid IS NULL`, `enabled = true`). Money **posts to the
   ledger / GL / register everywhere** — invoices + A/R, revenue recognition, settlements, expenses,
   bills, bill payments, customer payments, **factoring**, driver advances/escrow, bank feed + splits,
   parts, fuel-card overage, amortization, prepaid, fixed assets, lease, property tax, reimbursement,
   related-party loan, insurance-claim recovery, safety fine, TONU/cancellation A/R, transfers,
   warranty. Void-reversal is enabled. There is no "posting is off" state for USMCA.

2. **QuickBooks is the ONLY money exclusion — it stays OFF.** Keep disabled: every `QBO_*` flag
   (all sync / push / pull / mirror / projection), **`VOID_QBO_MIRROR_ENABLED`**, and
   **`TMS_QBO_RECON_ENABLED`**. This preserves the standing law **"Parallel books. No write-back to
   QuickBooks, ever. Reconcile only."** The read-only reconcile surfaces
   (`QBO_RECONCILE_UI_ENABLED`, `TMS_QBO_RECON_UI_ENABLED`) may remain on — they never write back.

3. **"Block" = the retired block-dispatch / audit-block queue.** It is dead, it is **not a flag**, and
   it is never resurrected (`Downloads/abb`, `Downloads/20 blocks`, GUARD-WORKORDERS sweep rows, etc.).

4. **New flags default ON for USMCA** unless the new flag is a QuickBooks / QBO write-back flag, in
   which case it defaults OFF. A seat adding a flag to `lib.feature_flags` must add the USMCA
   `enabled = true` override in the same change (or leave OFF only if it is a QBO write-back flag).

5. Owner-**action** gates are unchanged by this rule: enabling a *capability* flag (period close/reopen,
   opening-balance import, permission model) does not authorize a seat to perform the owner-only
   action. **Nobody closes a period but Jorge; opening balances are owner-entered; no seat moves money
   to an external system.** The flag being ON only makes the feature available in-app.

